y anti-colonial activism, Cold War-era marginalization, and sustained Kikuyu-Luo rivalry shaping Kenyan multiparty democracy. Culturally, the Luo are originators of benga and ohangla music. Unlike neighboring Nilotes (Kalenjin, Maasai), Luo do not practice male circumcision and historically removed six lower incisors as a distinctive ethnic marker.",', 'community': 'luo', 'section': 'section_0', 'relevance': 1.339097499847412, 'source': 'Luo.txt'}, {'content': '"embedding_context_hint": "Use for queries on Kenyan opposition politics, Nilotic migration patterns, Bantu-Nilotic admixture, East African music history, Cold War in Africa, African Nobel laureates, UNESCO heritage sites in Kenya, African diaspora achievement, and comparative ethnic studies (Luo/Kalenjin/Luhya)."\n}', 'community': 'luo', 'section': 'section_15', 'relevance': 1.4545384645462036, 'source': 'Luo.txt'}]}
