st Africa\'s intellectual, scientific, and professional classes. The community has produced outsized global figures: Barack Obama (44th US President), Lupita Nyong\'o (first black African Academy Award winner), Tom Mboya (Kenyan founding father), and Oginga Odinga (first Vice President). Luo political history is marked by early anti-colonial activism, Cold War-era marginalization, and sustained Kikuyu-Luo rivalry shaping Kenyan multiparty democracy. Culturally, the Luo are originators of benga and ohangla music. Unlike neighboring Nilotes (Kalenjin, Maasai), Luo do not practice male circumcision and historically removed six lower incisors as a distinctive ethnic marker.",', 'community': 'luo', 'section': 'section_0', 'relevance': 1.6516892910003662, 'source': 'Luo.txt'}]}
