| **Modern Scientific Reference** | In contemporary Luo discussions about astronomy, a person might refer to themselves as “the asteroid I am” when talking about their role in a space‑related project or a personal journey that feels “out of this world.” |
| **Creative Writing / Poetry** | A poet or songwriter could use the phrase to evoke imagery of speed, distance, or isolation. |

