ed in the Mau Mau uprising against British colonial rule. Senior Chief Muruatetu (16 wives, numerous descendants) exemplifies pre-colonial wealth (wives/children as riches) and colonial-era collaboration. The Embu are primarily agrarian, cultivating coffee, tea, muguka (khat), and macadamia as cash crops on some of Kenya\'s most fertile highlands, resulting in Embu County consistently ranking among Kenya\'s wealthiest counties with the longest life expectancy. Notable figures include Justin Muturi (Speaker of National Assembly 2013-2022), Cardinal John Njue, and Governor Cecily Mutitu Mbarire.",', 'context_blocks': [{'content': '"politics_and_governance": {\n    "gema_affiliation": "Embu are members of GEMA (Gikuyu-Embu-Meru-Akamba) community; political alliances with Kikuyu and Meru historically",\n    "colonial_chieftaincy": "Senior Chief Muruatetu — respected administration officer under colonial government and independent Kenya",\n    "contemporary_political_figures": [\n      "Justin Muturi (Speaker, National Assembly of Kenya, 2013-2022; former Attorney General-designate)",\n      "Cecily Mutitu Mbarire (Governor, Embu County; former MP, Runyenjes)",\n      "Martin Wambora (former Governor, Embu County; multiple terms; political longevity)",\n      "Jeremiah Nyagah (Member, pre-independence Legislative Council; Member, National Assembly of Kenya)",\n      "Joseph Nyagah (Kenyan politician; former Minister for Cooperative Development)",\n      "Njagi (son of Jeremiah Nyagah, continuation of political dynasty)"\n    ]\n  },', 'community': 'embu', 'relevance_score': 1.6556084156036377}, {'content': '"politics_and_governance": {\n    "gema_affiliation": "Embu are members of GEMA (Gikuyu-Embu-Meru-Akamba) community; political alliances with Kikuyu and Meru historically",\n    "colonial_chieftaincy": "Senior Chief Muruatetu — respected administration officer under colonial government and independent Kenya",\n    "contemporary_political_figures": [\n      "Justin Mut